# UK Transit Live - HTTPS front end.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews the Let's Encrypt certificate automatically.
# HTTPS is not cosmetic here: iOS Safari refuses geolocation and service
# workers over plain HTTP, which kills the "near me" feature and PWA install.
#
# The hostname is <reserved-ip>.sslip.io: sslip.io resolves the name to the
# embedded IP with no signup or DNS account. The IP is an OCI RESERVED public
# IP (free), so it survives instance rebuilds - re-attach it to a replacement
# VM and this exact config keeps working. Swap in a real domain later by
# changing this one line.
#
# This file is deployed by ci_deploy.sh to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile. Edit it here,
# not on the VM, or a rebuild silently reverts your change.
# Two hostnames, two independent wildcard-DNS providers (sslip.io and
# nip.io), one IP. Both are free volunteer-run services; if one has a DNS
# hiccup - which presents to a visitor as "the site is down" while the server
# is fine - the other URL keeps working. Caddy holds a certificate for each.
145.241.199.54.sslip.io, 145.241.199.54.nip.io {
    encode zstd gzip
    reverse_proxy localhost:8620
}
